#html.p(id: "en-N034")[#text("34 There are two other Balinese values and disvalues which, connected with punctuate temporality on the one hand and unbridled aggressiveness on the other, reinforce the sense that the cockfight is at once continuous with ordinary social life and a direct negation of it: what the Balinese call ramé, and what they call paling. Ramé means crowded, noisy, and active, and is a highly sought-after social state: crowded markets, mass festivals, busy streets are all ramé as, of course, is, in the extreme, a cockfight. Ramé is what happens in the “full” times (its opposite, sepi, “quiet,” is what happens in the “empty” ones). Paling is social vertigo, the dizzy, disoriented, lost, turned-around feeling one gets when one’s place in the coordinates of social space is not clear, and it is a tremendously disfavored, immensely anxiety-producing state. Balinese regard the exact maintenance of spatial orientation (“not to know where north is” is to be crazy), balance, decorum, status relationships, and so forth, as fundamental to ordered life (krama) and paling, the sort of whirling confusion of position the scrambling cocks exemplify as its profoundest enemy and contradiction. On ramé see Bateson and Mead, Balinese Character, 3, 64; on paling, ibid., 11, and Belo, ed., Traditional Balinese Culture, 90ff.")]

#zh(id: "N034")[#text("34 巴厘岛还有另外两种价值观和贬义，它们一方面与不经意的时间性有关，另一方面与肆无忌惮的侵略性有关，强化了这样一种感觉：斗鸡既是普通社会生活的延续，又是对它的直接否定：巴厘岛人称之为“ramé”，以及他们所说的“paling”。 Ramé的意思是拥挤、喧闹、活跃，是一种备受追捧的社会状态：拥挤的市场、大型节日、繁忙的街道都是ramé，当然，极端的斗鸡也是如此。 Ramé 是在“充实”的时候发生的事情（它的反面，sepi，“安静”，是在​​“空”的时候发生的事情）。失落是一种社交眩晕症，当一个人在社会空间的坐标中的位置不明确时，就会产生头晕、迷失方向、迷失、转身的感觉，这是一种非常不受欢迎、非常令人焦虑的状态。巴厘岛人将空间方位的精确维持（“不知道北方在哪里”是疯狂的）、平衡、礼仪、地位关系等视为有序生活（krama）的基础，而攀爬公鸡所体现的那种旋转的位置混乱则是其最深刻的敌人和矛盾。关于 ramé，请参阅 Bateson 和 Mead，巴厘岛性格，3, 64； on paling，同上，11，以及 Belo 编辑，传统巴厘岛文化，90ff。")]

#html.p(id: "en-N035")[#text("35 The Stevens reference is to his “The Motive for Metaphor,” (“You like it under the trees in autumn, / Because everything is half dead. / The wind moves like a cripple among the leaves / And repeats words without meaning”); the Schoenberg reference is to the third of his Five Orchestral Pieces (Opus 16), and is borrowed from H. H. Drager, “The Concept of ‘Tonal Body,’” in Susanne Langer, ed., Reflections on Art (New York: Oxford University Press, 1961), 174. On Hogarth, and on this whole problem– there called “multiple matrix matching”–see E. H. Gombrich, “The Use of Art for the Study of Symbols,” in James Hogg, ed., Psychology and the Visual Arts (Baltimore: Penguin Brooks, 1969), 149–170. The more usual term for this sort of semantic alchemy is “metaphorical transfer,” and good technical discussions of it can be found in M. Black, Models and Metaphors (Ithaca, N.Y.: Cornell University Press, 1962), 25ff; Goodman, Language as Art, 44ff; and W. Percy, “Metaphor as Mistake,” Sewanee Review 66 (1958): 78–99.")]

#zh(id: "N035")[#text("35 史蒂文斯提到了他的“隐喻的动机”（“你喜欢秋天的树下，/因为一切都半死不活。/风像跛子一样在树叶间移动/并重复毫无意义的话语”）；勋伯格参考的是他的五首管弦乐作品中的第三首（作品 16），借用自 H. H. Drager，“‘音体’的概念”，收录于 Susanne Langer 编辑，Reflections on Art（纽约：牛津大学出版社，1961 年），174。符号的研究”，詹姆斯·霍格主编，心理学和视觉艺术（巴尔的摩：企鹅布鲁克斯，1969），149-170。这种语义炼金术的更常用术语是“隐喻转移”，有关它的良好技术讨论可以在 M. Black, Models and Metaphors (Ithaca, N.Y.: Cornell University Press, 1962), 25ff 中找到；古德曼，《语言作为艺术》，第 44 页；以及 W. Percy，“隐喻是错误”，Sewanee Review 66 (1958)：78-99。")]

#html.p(id: "en-N036")[#text("36 The tag is from the second book of the Organon, On Interpretation. For a discussion of it, and for the whole argument for freeing “the notion of text . . . from the notion of scripture or writing,” and constructing, thus, a general hermeneutics, see Paul Ricoeur, Freud and Philosophy (New Haven, Conn.: Yale University Press, 1970), 20ff.")]

#zh(id: "N036")[#text("36 该标签来自《欧加农》的第二本书《论解释》。对于它的讨论，以及关于将“文本的概念……从圣经或写作的概念中解放出来”并因此构建一般解释学的整个论证，请参见保罗·利科，《弗洛伊德与哲学》（康涅狄格州纽黑文：耶鲁大学出版社，1970），20ff。")]

