#html.p(id: "en-N038")[#text("38 Lévi-Strauss’s “structuralism” might seem an exception. But it is only an apparent one, for, rather than taking myths, totem rites, marriage rules, or whatever as texts to interpret, Lévi-Strauss takes them as ciphers to solve, which is very much not the same thing. He does not seek to understand symbolic forms in terms of how they function in concrete situations to organize perceptions (meanings, emotions, concepts, attitudes); he seeks to understand them entirely in terms of their internal structure, indépendent de tout sujet, de tout objet, et de toute contexte. For my own view of this approach–that is suggestive and indefensible– see Clifford Geertz, “The Cerebral Savage: On the Work of Lévi-Strauss,” Encounter 48 (1967): 25–32.")]

#zh(id: "N038")[#text("38 列维-斯特劳斯的“结构主义”似乎是一个例外。但这只是表面上的一个，因为列维-斯特劳斯不是把神话、图腾仪式、婚姻规则或其他任何东西当作文本来解释，而是把它们当作密码来解决，这完全不是一回事。他并不试图从符号形式在具体情境中如何发挥作用来组织感知（意义、情感、概​​念、态度）来理解它们；而是试图理解符号形式。他力求完全从其内部结构、独立的总体、总体对象和总体背景的角度来理解它们。对于我自己对这种方法的看法——这是有启发性的和站不住脚的——请参阅 Clifford Geertz, “The Cerebral Savage: On the Work of Lévi-Strauss,” Encounter 48 (1967): 25-32。")]

#html.p(id: "en-N039")[#text("39 Frye, The Educated Imagination, 63–64.")]

#zh(id: "N039")[#text("39 弗莱，《受过教育的想象力》，63-64。")]

#html.p(id: "en-N040")[#text("40 The use of the, to Europeans, “natural” visual idiom for perception–“see,” “watches,” and so forth–is more than usually misleading here, for the fact that, as mentioned earlier, Balinese follow the progress of the fight as much (perhaps, as fighting cocks are actually rather hard to see except as blurs of motion, more) with their bodies as with their eyes, moving their limbs, heads, and trunks in gestural mimicry of the cocks’ maneuvers, means that much of the individual’s experience of the fight is kinesthetic rather than visual. If ever there was an example of Kenneth Burke’s definition of a symbolic act as “the dancing of an attitude” (The Philosophy of Literary Form, rev. ed. [New York: Vintage Books, 1957], 9) the cockfight is it. On the enormous role of kinesthetic perception in Balinese life, Bateson and Mead, Balinese Character, 84–88; on the active nature of aesthetic perception in general, Goodman, Language of Art, 241–244.")]

#zh(id: "N040")[#text("40 对于欧洲人来说，使用“自然”的视觉习语来表达感知——“看”、“手表”等等——在这里比通常情况下更具有误导性，因为事实上，正如前面提到的，巴厘岛人不仅用眼睛来跟踪战斗的进展（也许，斗鸡实际上很难看到，除了运动模糊之外），用他们的身体和眼睛来移动他们的四肢、头部和躯干，模仿斗鸡的动作。公鸡的动作，意味着个人对战斗的大部分体验是动觉的，而不是视觉的。如果肯尼思·伯克将象征性行为定义为“一种态度的舞蹈”（《文学形式哲学》，修订版。[纽约：古着图书，1957]，9），那么斗鸡就是它了。关于动觉知觉在巴厘岛人生活中的巨大作用，贝特森和米德，巴厘岛性格，84-88；关于一般审美知觉的主动本质，古德曼，《艺术语言》，241-244。")]

#html.p(id: "en-N041")[#text("41 All this coupling of the occidental great with the oriental lowly will doubtless disturb certain sorts of aestheticians as the earlier efforts of anthropologists to speak of Christianity and totemism in the same breath disturbed certain sorts of theologians. But as ontological questions are (or should be) bracketed in the sociology of religion, judgmental ones are (or should be) bracketed in the sociology of art. In any case, the attempt to deprovincialize the concept of art is but part of the general anthropological conspiracy to deprovincialize all important social concepts–marriage, religion, law, rationality–and though this is a threat to aesthetic theories which regard certain works of art as beyond the reach of sociological analysis, it is no threat to the conviction, for which Robert Graves claims to have been reprimanded at his Cambridge tripos, that some poems are better than others.")]

#zh(id: "N041")[#text("41所有这些西方伟人与东方卑人的结合无疑会扰乱某些类型的美学家，就像人类学家早期将基督教和图腾崇拜相提并论的努力扰乱了某些类型的神学家一样。但是，正如本体论问题被（或应该）包含在宗教社会学中一样，判断性问题也被（或应该）包含在艺术社会学中。无论如何，试图去地方化艺术概念只是人类学阴谋的一部分，目的是去地方化所有重要的社会概念——婚姻、宗教、法律、理性——尽管这对美学理论构成了威胁，因为美学理论认为某些艺术作品超出了社会学分析的范围，但它并没有威胁到罗伯特·格雷夫斯声称在剑桥三人组中受到斥责的信念，即有些诗比其他诗更好。")]

#html.p(id: "en-N042")[#text("42 For the consecration ceremony, see V. E. Korn, “The Consecration of the Priest,” in Swellengrebel, ed., Bali, 131–154; for (somewhat exaggerated) village communion, Roelof Goris, “The Religious Character of the Balinese Village,” ibid., 79–100.")]

#zh(id: "N042")[#text("42 关于祝圣仪式，参见 V. E. Korn，《牧师的祝圣》，Swellengrebel 编辑，巴厘岛，131-154；对于（有点夸张的）村庄共融，Roelof Goris，“巴厘岛村庄的宗教特征”，同上，79-100。")]

#html.p(id: "en-N043")[#text("43 That what the cockfight has to say about Bali is not altogether without perception and the disquiet it expresses about the general pattern of Balinese life is not wholly without reason is attested by the fact that in two weeks of December 1965, during the upheavals following the unsuccessful coup in Djakarta, between forty and eighty thousand Balinese (in a population of about two million) were killed, largely by one another–the worst outburst in the country. (John Hughes, Indonesian Upheaval [New York: McKay, 1967], 173–183. Hughes’s figures are, of course, rather casual estimates, but they are not the most extreme.) This is not to say, of course, that the killings were caused by the cockfight, could have been predicted on the basis of it, or were some sort of enlarged version of it with real people in the place of the cocks–all of which is nonsense. It is merely to say that if one looks at Bali not just through the medium of its dances, its shadowplays, its sculpture, and its girls, but–as the Balinese themselves do–also through the medium of its cockfight, the fact that the massacre occurred seems, if no less appalling, less like a contradiction to the laws of nature. As more than one real Gloucester has discovered, sometimes people actually get life precisely as they most deeply do not want it.")]

#zh(id: "N043")[#text("43 斗鸡对巴厘岛的描述并非完全没有感知，它所表达的对巴厘岛人普遍生活模式的不安也并非完全没有道理，这一点可以从以下事实得到证明：1965 年 12 月的两周内，雅加达政变未成功后发生的动乱中，有 40 至 8 万名巴厘岛人（人口约 200 万）被杀害，其中大部分是互相杀害——这是巴厘岛历史上最严重的一次爆发。国家。 （约翰·休斯，印度尼西亚剧变[纽约：麦凯，1967]，173-183。当然，休斯的数字是相当随意的估计，但它们并不是最极端的。）当然，这并不是说杀戮是由斗鸡引起的，可以根据斗鸡进行预测，或者是斗鸡的某种放大版本，用真人代替斗鸡——所有这些都是废话。这只是说，如果人们不仅通过舞蹈、皮影戏、雕塑和女孩来看待巴厘岛，而且像巴厘岛人自己一样，也通过斗鸡这一媒介来看待巴厘岛，那么发生大屠杀的事实即使不那么令人震惊，也不像与自然法则的矛盾。正如不止一位真正的格洛斯特所发现的那样，有时人们实际上得到的生活恰恰是他们最不想要的。")]
